@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN. P17-ASSEMBLY-001's
rem and P17-SOLVE-001's copies each carried bare OLD_END lines -- leaked
rem heredoc terminators -- which cmd.exe reported into their .err files.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-VIZ-001 -- FEA Visualisation / Inspection. The exact invocation,
rem recorded so the run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, TWENTY-THREE in a row counting this one.
rem verify-harness.cmd beside it is its regression and was not edited.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem                        sha1sum         244b38de8feac0475af7cdc56ba9415d27d8dd29
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem                        sha1sum         afd0197d4f4726db7f533c2f27f4f6e069ba83c6
rem
rem BOTH FORMS ARE RECORDED because they differ and a hash without its
rem algorithm cannot be checked: .gitattributes sets `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, so
rem git stores LF while the working tree is CRLF. A note carrying only the
rem git-blob value makes a sha1sum check fail against a harness that is
rem correct, and this milestone lost ten minutes to exactly that.
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: this machine has 16 logical cores, so `cmake --build` lets Ninja
rem run 18 compiles at once, and a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy
rem translation units exhausted the commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens
rem nothing: the same sources, the same flags, -Werror included; the no-op
rem rebuild check still proves the binaries are the ones just built; the full
rem suite still runs unfiltered in all three presets. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT CHANGED, AND WHAT IS OWED BY IT.
rem
rem   NEW          include/bettercad/renderer/StructuralResultView.hpp
rem                include/bettercad/renderer/StructuralInspection.hpp
rem                include/bettercad/renderer/StructuralContour.hpp
rem                src/renderer/StructuralResultView.cpp
rem                src/renderer/StructuralInspection.cpp
rem                src/renderer/StructuralContour.cpp
rem                tests/renderer/StructuralResultViewTests.cpp
rem   MODIFIED     src/renderer/CMakeLists.txt       three sources and one
rem                                                  new PUBLIC_LINK
rem                tests/CMakeLists.txt              one registration
rem                include/bettercad/structural/StructuralValidation.hpp
rem                src/structural/StructuralValidation.cpp
rem
rem A PREDECESSOR WAS MODIFIED, and this run is what pays for it.
rem StructuralSolveOutcome gained `fields` and `reactions`. P17-VALID-001
rem computed both one statement earlier and discarded them, and the viewer
rem needs them because StructuralResult stores Strain6 and Stress6 but NOT
rem von Mises, the principal stresses, the principal strains, the hydrostatic
rem stress or |u| -- so a viewer restricted to the published result would have
rem to recompute them, which is the duplicate numerical authority this
rem milestone is forbidden to create. The change is additive and computes
rem nothing new. P17-VALID-001 IS REQUALIFIED BY THIS RUN; that debt was
rem recorded as outstanding and is discharged here, not assumed away.
rem
rem THE RENDERER MODULE GAINED A DEPENDENCY: BetterCAD::structural, PUBLIC,
rem because StructuralResultView.hpp takes a RecoveredFields and hands back
rem Stress and Length. renderer is layer 70 and structural is 50, so the arrow
rem points downward and architecture.layering is in the repeat set to say so.
rem
rem NO SHARED TEST INFRASTRUCTURE CHANGED. tests/architecture/CheckLayering.cmake
rem is byte-identical to P17-VALID-001's.
rem
rem ONE WHITESPACE-ONLY CORRECTION: src/renderer/CMakeLists.txt was CRLF in
rem the working tree while HEAD has it pure LF and .gitattributes says
rem `* text=auto eol=lf`. An earlier session's edit converted it. Normalised
rem back to LF with a content check that failed on anything but the carriage
rem returns. git diff shows only the four intended lines.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. 937 tests, counted with ctest -N
rem against this filter in debug-ext, not estimated:
rem
rem   unit\.Structural         covers unit.StructuralViz as a substring, so
rem                            this milestone's 33 are here -- VERIFIED by
rem                            ctest -N -R 'unit\.StructuralViz' returning 33
rem                            and by the suite total moving from 3759 to
rem                            3792, the two ends agreeing on 33. Plus the
rem                            whole P17 chain, every member of which this
rem                            milestone reads: VALID, REACTION, POST, SOLVE,
rem                            ASSEMBLY, BC, LOAD, ELEM, MAT, DATA, ARCH.
rem                            P17-VALID's requalification lives here.
rem   unit\.Mesh               covers MeshView (13), MeshDisplay (15),
rem                            MeshScene (9), MeshHighlight (9) and MeshDofMap
rem                            as substrings. ALL FOUR RENDERER PREFIXES ARE
rem                            THE BASIS OF THIS MILESTONE: MeshView supplies
rem                            the render buffers and the index-to-id bridge,
rem                            MeshScene is where a type-name collision this
rem                            milestone introduced was found, MeshHighlight
rem                            is the path both new highlight entry points
rem                            delegate to, and MeshDisplay owns the single
rem                            metres-to-millimetres conversion.
rem   unit\.View               Viewer (22), View (23) and ViewProjection (15).
rem                            THE ADDITION OVER P17-VALID'S SET, +68 tests:
rem                            the renderer library they exercise is the one
rem                            that gained three sources and a new public
rem                            dependency.
rem   unit\.Quality            P16-QUALITY's. Carried because P17-VALID-001's
rem                            acceptance policy is requalified by this run
rem                            and its thresholds are QualityThresholds values
rem                            consumed by evaluateMeshQuality.
rem   unit\.MeshDofMap, unit\.ConstraintSet, unit\.FreeEquationMap
rem                            P17-DOF's, carried for P17-VALID's sake: the
rem                            constrained-degree-of-freedom count is a
rem                            refusal there.
rem   unit\.Tet4Element        P17-ELEM's. The accuracy laws P17-VALID derives
rem                            are measured through recoverElementFields, and
rem                            every channel this milestone reads is one of
rem                            its stored outputs.
rem   unit\.Volume, unit\.Tet  P16's enumeration, node positions and signed
rem                            volume -- the order every field in this
rem                            milestone is published in.
rem   unit\.Siz                P16-SIZE's. The viewer fixture drives a 20 mm
rem                            global target with a 6 mm local control, and
rem                            that control is what gives the mesh interior
rem                            nodes at all.
rem   unit\.Id                 the identity machinery. This milestone carries
rem                            NodeId and ElementId arrays parallel to every
rem                            field rather than positional indices.
rem   architecture             containment and layering over the whole tree,
rem                            and the reason it matters here is the new
rem                            renderer-to-structural edge.
rem   unit\.ReferenceModel     the twelve mechanical parts (P11/P12).
rem   unit\.Analytic           the independent geometry toolkit's own tests.
rem   refmod\.                 every reference-model process test.
rem   gui\.                    the application links the renderer, which is
rem                            the library this milestone changed.
rem
rem NOT in the set: unit\.Unit and unit\.Quantity (no unit-system change),
rem unit\.Material and unit\.Mass (no material code changed), and the drawing
rem and assembly view tests, which link the renderer but were not touched by
rem it -- a link-order or symbol problem there is caught by the UNFILTERED run
rem in all three presets, which is where a change nobody predicted shows up.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem eleven milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so repeating
rem one measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's. They still
rem run UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
